2026-09-30T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2291) 'A verb is an atom and its row text is kebab, so `:may_use` reads as `may-use` in a row and in a table. `capability` defaults its verb to its own name and takes `object:` and `caveats:`. `relate` takes an optional note, which renders after `#` the way a denial's reason does.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2291  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-30T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2291) 'What is checked, and when
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2291  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-30T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2291) '`RFD.ReBAC.problems/2` is the one implementation of every rule, and both the DSL and the gate call it. A block's shape is checked while its source compiles, so a bad declaration is a compile error that names the rule:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2291  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-30T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2291) '- each segment is lowercase kebab, and each verb is declared once with a meaning
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2291  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-30T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2291) '- a denial carries its reason
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2291  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-30T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2291) '- no row repeats, and no relation is both granted and denied
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2291  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-30T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2291) '- a capability names one verb on one object and states its caveats once
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2291  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-30T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2291) 'The vocabulary is the exception. A `verbs_from` resolves only once every source is loaded, so `mix rfd.rebac` holds every block and every fenced document block against the verbs the corpus declares. The two halves together are what the regex read before.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2291  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-30T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2291) 'The rendering is the evidence
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2291  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-30T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2291) 'The fenced block rendered into `CLAUDE.md` from RFD66606-2200's nine rows came out byte for byte the block that was there, reasons aligned in their column included. A rendering that differs from the prose it replaces means the declarations are wrong, not the prose, and that is the check worth running on each further migration.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2291  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-30T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2291) 'What the migration found
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2291  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-30T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2291) 'Two verbs are used by RFDs that RFD66606-2200 never named, which a vocabulary read out of one table could not report:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2291  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-30T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2291) '- `trusts`, which RFD66606-2239 (traits and one binary) states as an amendment to RFD66606-2200.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2291  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-30T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2291) '- `role` and `may-use`, which RFD66606-2202 and `rectgtn/fleet.jsonld` both use. `CLAUDE.md` happens to use neither, so the gate never looked at a row carrying one.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2291  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-30T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-2291) 'All three are `verb` lines in RFD66606-2200 now, which is what RFD66606-2200's own rule asks for: a new verb is an amendment to that RFD before it is a row anywhere.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2291  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-30T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-2291) 'What this does not do
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2291  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-30T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-2291) 'Enforcement is unchanged. RFD66606-2200's tuples are still data, Bao identity groups still enforce the role rows (RFD66606-2202), and the macaroons of RFD66606-2288 are still a design. The live tuples are Bao KV rows under `relationships/`, and an RFD declares only the rows it states itself.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2291  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-30T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-2291) 'The planner's own ReBAC engine is untouched: `tw_rebac.hpp`'s relation types, the Lean specification over them and `capabilities` in a RECTGTN domain are a separate vocabulary with a separate check.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2291  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-30T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-2291) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2291  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-30T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-2291) '`scripts/check_rebac.exs` read its verb vocabulary by matching pipes in RFD66606-2200's rendered Markdown table, and RFD66606-2232 (the RFD DSL) makes that Markdown a build artifact.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2291  1 LINE
 Text:Written
